From 0ff57dd922520e4a1837102f77d5e3878a8a27b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:55:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] transports: add /api/platform/tenants admin handlers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the TenantRepository CRUD primitives from patch 0011 into the
HTTP transport so the platform-admin control plane can manage tenants
end-to-end:

  GET    /api/platform/tenants                  list + paging + filters
  POST   /api/platform/tenants                  create
  GET    /api/platform/tenants/{tenant_id}      get one
  PUT    /api/platform/tenants/{tenant_id}      partial update
  DELETE /api/platform/tenants/{tenant_id}      delete (with guards)

Routes live under /api/platform rather than /api/governance because
tenants sit above the governance hierarchy and the access-control
layer needs to gate them with platform-admin-only auth (cross-tenant)
once the RBAC layer lands.

Status codes wired through to the store-level errors:
  - 400 on missing/invalid fields, invalid status, malformed JSON
  - 404 on ErrNotFound (Get/Update/Delete of missing id)
  - 409 on ErrAlreadyExists (Create with duplicate id)
  - 409 on ErrReservedTenant (Delete of DefaultTenantID)
  - 409 on ErrTenantNotEmpty (Delete with dependents)
  - 201 Created on successful Create
  - 200 OK on every other success

Update is a partial PUT: only fields supplied in the body overwrite
the existing row (Name / Status / Description). ID is immutable.

New handler file (handlers/tenants.go) plus 12 HTTP-level tests in
handlers/tenants_test.go that spin up a real SQLite-backed
ConfigStore via configstore.NewConfigStore — exercising the actual
migration chain so the default tenant is seeded and tenant_id
columns are present everywhere.

Wired in server.go alongside the other admin handlers, behind the
shared middlewares chain. Tightening to platform-admin-only auth is
a follow-up that depends on the RBAC layer.

All test suites still pass:
  - framework/configstore
  - plugins/governance
  - multitenant
  - transports/bifrost-http/handlers (12 new TestTenantsHandler_*)

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
